Boosting — Summary & Practical Implementation
This section of the course explores Boosting, an ensemble meta-algorithm that builds an ensemble sequentially by training each base model (usually shallow decision trees, or CARTs) to correct the errors made by the previous models.

🚀 Key Concepts & Techniques Learned
1. AdaBoost (Adaptive Boosting)
Mechanism: In AdaBoost, each subsequent tree is trained on the weighted training dataset, where misclassified instances from the previous tree are assigned higher weights so the next tree focuses hard on them.

Prediction: Final predictions are determined via weighted majority vote (for classification) or weighted sum (for regression).

Evaluation: Scored binary classifiers using metrics like ROC AUC (roc_auc_score from sklearn.metrics).

2. Gradient Boosting (GB)
Mechanism: Instead of adjusting sample weights like AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting sequentially fits new trees to the residual errors (pseudo-residuals) of the prior predictions, using gradient descent optimization.

Key Hyperparameters:

max_depth: Controls the depth of each individual regression tree (typically set to shallow values like 3 or 4).

n_estimators: Defines the number of boosting stages (trees) to build.

3. Stochastic Gradient Boosting (SGB)
Mechanism: To mitigate overfitting and add diversity to the ensemble, Stochastic Gradient Boosting introduces randomization at each boosting step:

Subsampling (subsample): Each tree is trained on a fraction (e.g., 90%) of the available training data.

Max Features (max_features): Each tree considers a random subset of features when looking for the best split.

Performance: Typically yields better generalization and lowers test set RMSE compared to standard gradient boosting.

💻 Code Snippets & Quick Reference
Training & Evaluating AdaBoost Classifier
Python
from sklearn.ensemble import AdaBoostClassifier
from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score

# Instantiate and fit AdaBoost classifier
ada = AdaBoostClassifier(n_estimators=200, random_state=2)
ada.fit(X_train, y_train)

# Predict probabilities for the positive class
y_pred_proba = ada.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]

# Evaluate ROC AUC score
ada_roc_auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_pred_proba)
print('ROC AUC score: {:.2f}'.format(ada_roc_auc))
Training & Evaluating Gradient Boosting Regressor
Python
from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingRegressor
from sklearn.metrics import mean_squared_error as MSE

# Instantiate and fit Gradient Boosting Regressor
gb = GradientBoostingRegressor(max_depth=4, n_estimators=200, random_state=2)
gb.fit(X_train, y_train)

# Predict and compute RMSE
y_pred = gb.predict(X_test)
rmse_test = MSE(y_test, y_pred)**(1/2)
print('Test set RMSE of gb: {:.3f}'.format(rmse_test))
